Description: Refuse a password change with a password that is not valid UTF-8
 A password that is not valid UTF-8 converted to NULL. A NULL old password
 asks opendirectoryd to set the password without checking the old one, and
 opendirectoryd allows that for root. So a password change that a program
 running as root made through this module did not check an old password
 that was not valid UTF-8.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-17

--- a/modules/pam_opendirectory/pam_opendirectory.m
+++ b/modules/pam_opendirectory/pam_opendirectory.m
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
  */
